# .punused-ignore — adjudicated punused findings.
#
# The CI gate runs punused per directory, then matches every finding line
# against the literal substrings in this file. A finding that matches nothing
# fails the build; an entry that matches nothing warns as stale. Full-line "#"
# comments carry the reason.
#
# punused (github.com/bep/punused) drives gopls and reports two codes:
#   EU1002 "is unused"            — gopls found ZERO references.
#   EU1001 "is used in test only" — every reference is in a _test.go file.
# Its reference view is one Go module with default build tags, so it cannot see
# cross-language consumers (the generated TypeScript client), callers inside an
# external library that dials back into our interface, reflection dispatch, or
# an interface member load-bearing only through interface-to-interface
# assignment.
#
# An entry is an adjudication, not an amnesty: adding one means the symbol was
# checked and defended. Real dead code gets deleted instead.
#
# This file is INCOMPLETE. vibekit carries a large unadjudicated backlog that
# the spec's final task works through; entries land here as they are defended.

# --- Test-isolation seam that prevents writing the developer's own $HOME ------
